Things that went wrong and what I did them. I'm keeping this because the troubleshooting
has taught me more that the parts that worked first time. 

Kali wouldnt install on ARM64
I downloaded kali-linux-2026.1-installer-arm64.iso, which is the correct architecture for an M-series Mac. 
Both the graphical installer and the plain one died the same way. 
The ISO being the right architecture is what made this annoyinh because thats the obvious thing to check and it wasnt the problem. 
From what I could work out the error is about how the installer's kernel sees the Virtual hardware UTM is preseting it. 

The decision I made was to stop. I'd already spent longer on it than the VM was worth, and the machine was never the interesting part of this project.
Swapping to Ubuntu and installing the four or five tools 
I actually needed took about ten minutes and unblocked everything.

LOCKED OUT of both VMs: 
I came back to this after a few months off and couldnt remember either password.
Nothing in a password manager, nothing written down anywhere. 

Trying GRUB first: 
The normal way to fix this is catch the GRUB menu while it's booting, pick recovery mode, 
and reset the password from the robot shell it gives you. I couldnt catch it. The timeout in this VM
is very short, and holding Shift or Esc buttons just dropped me back to the firmware meny instead which is a layer below GRUB. 

I booted from the instaler instead, booted the VM off an Ubuntu server ISO, got a shell in the live environment and mounted
both the VMs real disk from outside it. 
Then I could change the password on the actual installed system without ever booting it. 

